  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the kitten in the box scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the kitten, as the text 'when your kitten can't find a box' uses the possessive 'your', directly addressing the viewer as the owner of the kitten. This creates an identification where the user sees themselves as the 'you' in the scenario, experiencing the kitten's imagined frustration. The visual of the kitten peeking out of the box reinforces this projection by making the viewer empathize with the kitten's situation as if it were their own pet's experience.",
